data: {"type":"data-vendo-build-failed","data":{"toolCallId":"hcall_4_4f8601c0-9420-483d-9c5b-c7290ebd73e9","reason":"app build failed: This app wasn't created, because it didn't pass the checks that keep an app honest: The entire metric grid failed to build ('This section could not be built — retry the edit'), so the current balance, $2,000 threshold, last-checked time, and alert status are never rendered — these must be bound to accounts.data[0].balance (÷100 for dollars), a static $2,000 threshold label, a real timestamp, and a conditional OK/Below Threshold derived from the balance. The trend/sparkline and last-checked section also failed to build ('This section could not be built — retry the edit'), so MapleSparkline is never rendered and the last-checked time is never shown — these must be bound to accounts.data[0].sparkline and a real last-checked timestamp. The prominent in-app alert when balance < $2,000 is never shown: the checking account balance is 941220 cents ($9,412.20) in the sample data but the app has no conditional alert component at all — an Alert/Banner should be rendered conditionally when accounts.data[0].balance < 200000, displaying the current balance in dollars. The app uses host_listNotifications to derive alert status, but that query lists generic user notifications (paycheck, card swipe, security) — it does not return a computed below-threshold status; the alert status (OK vs Below Threshold) must be derived directly by comparing accounts.data[0].balance to 200000, not inferred from notification records."}}

data: {"type":"tool-output-error","toolCallId":"hcall_4_4f8601c0-9420-483d-9c5b-c7290ebd73e9","errorText":"app build failed: This app wasn't created, because it didn't pass the checks that keep an app honest: The entire metric grid failed to build ('This section could not be built — retry the edit'), so the current balance, $2,000 threshold, last-checked time, and alert status are never rendered — these must be bound to accounts.data[0].balance (÷100 for dollars), a static $2,000 threshold label, a real timestamp, and a conditional OK/Below Threshold derived from the balance. The trend/sparkline and last-checked section also failed to build ('This section could not be built — retry the edit'), so MapleSparkline is never rendered and the last-checked time is never shown — these must be bound to accounts.data[0].sparkline and a real last-checked timestamp. The prominent in-app alert when balance < $2,000 is never shown: the checking account balance is 941220 cents ($9,412.20) in the sample data but the app has no conditional alert component at all — an Alert/Banner should be rendered conditionally when accounts.data[0].balance < 200000, displaying the current balance in dollars. The app uses host_listNotifications to derive alert status, but that query lists generic user notifications (paycheck, card swipe, security) — it does not return a computed below-threshold status; the alert status (OK vs Below Threshold) must be derived directly by comparing accounts.data[0].balance to 200000, not inferred from notification records.","dynamic":true}

